   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT relating to establishing the power plant tax assessment challenge\nreserve fund",
    "basePrintNo": "S7105",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7105-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7105\n\nSPONSOR: MATTERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to establishing the power plant tax assessment challenge\nreserve fund\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nEstablishes the Northport-East Northport LIPA power plant tax assessment\nchallenge reserve fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: The education law is amended by adding a new section 36.\n\nSection 2: Identifies effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTax certiorari challenges present a significant obstacle for our local\ngovernments and school districts in their ability to remain fiscally\nstable. When faced with a tax certiorari challenge, these entities must\ndecide whether to negotiate a settlement and suffer potentially large\nlosses in revenue, or to progress with costly legal proceedings. Adverse\njudgments of this magnitude could have a crippling effect on taxpayers.\nTowns and districts could be forced to cut services and programs that\nare desperately needed by residents and our children. Allowing school\ndistricts, the ability to plan for such challenges will protect taxpay-\ners. This bill will help decrease the impact of such settlements or\nadverse judgments if, and when, they arise.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
